WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.580
How does Bellman-Ford work? Relax

2
00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.600
every directed edge repeatedly, allowing

3
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.240
negative weights and checking for

4
00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.480
reachable negative cycles. It is

5
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.980
deliberately systematic, which is occasionally

6
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.540
more useful than trying to

7
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:13.960
be clever.

8
00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.380
Start with distance zero at

9
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:19.260
S and infinity elsewhere. Relaxing

10
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.600
u to v tests whether

11
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.080
distance u plus the edge

12
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.520
weight is smaller than distance

13
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.280
v; on improvement, update both

14
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:27.660
the distance and its parent.

15
00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:29.640
Our chain is S to

16
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.040
A with weight two, A

17
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.120
to B with negative one,

18
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.500
then B to T with

19
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.820
five. Scan edges backwards each

20
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.560
pass: B to T, A

21
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.820
to B, S to A.

22
00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:41.040
In pass one, B and

23
00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.860
A still have infinite distances

24
00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.260
when their outgoing edges are

25
00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:46.160
checked. Only the last edge,

26
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.007
S to A, improves a

27
00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.260
label, setting A to two.

28
00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:51.920
In pass two, B to

29
00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.100
T still cannot improve anything.

30
00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.800
A to B now offers

31
00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.680
two minus one, so B

32
00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.780
becomes one; S to A

33
00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.320
leaves its label unchanged.

34
00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:03.480
In pass three, B to

35
00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.380
T offers one plus five,

36
00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:08.260
giving T distance six. We

37
00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:10.320
now know the route S,

38
00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:10.860
A, B, T, and its

39
00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.515
parent pointers reconstruct that route

40
00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:13.380
backwards.

41
00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.680
After k full passes, every

42
00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.280
vertex with a finite shortest

43
00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:19.940
path using at most k

44
00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:21.560
edges has its correct distance.

45
00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.880
An in-place scan may propagate

46
00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.880
farther within one pass, so

47
00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:27.800
k is a guarantee, not

48
00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:28.700
an exact limit.

49
00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.520
Without a reachable negative cycle,

50
00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.620
a finite shortest route can

51
00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:35.560
be chosen simple, using at

52
00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.140
most n minus one edges.

53
00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:40.140
That explains the n minus

54
00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:41.320
one complete passes; a whole

55
00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.960
unchanged pass permits early stopping.

56
00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:47.700
After those passes, an additional

57
00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.480
scan checks for any improvement

58
00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.980
from a finite-distance tail. An

59
00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:54.020
improvement certifies a negative cycle

60
00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:56.420
reachable from S; the improving

61
00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.200
edge itself may merely be

62
00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.620
downstream of that cycle.

63
00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.280
With n vertices and m

64
00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.880
edges, there are at most

65
00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:05.820
n minus one full scans

66
00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:08.915
of m edges, plus initialisation

67
00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.060
and the detection scan. This

68
00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:12.940
gives order n plus n

69
00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:14.940
m time and order n

70
00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.780
auxiliary labels and parents.

71
00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.000
Things to take note of.

72
00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.500
Negative edges are allowed, but

73
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.240
a reachable negative cycle can

74
00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.260
make distances unbounded below for

75
00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.940
targets it can reach. A

76
00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.760
disconnected negative cycle does not

77
00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:30.240
affect this source’s distances.

78
00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.420
Skip numeric relaxation from infinity

79
00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.280
and respect the specified edge

80
00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.400
order when tracing. A singleton

81
00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.100
needs no ordinary pass but

82
00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.440
still needs the cycle check

83
00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.600
for a negative self-loop. Repeated

84
00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.500
relaxation needs a stopping argument,

85
00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.360
and now you have one.
